Acceptance criteria

The work is complete only when the following player-visible sequence works:

A human player has Combat Assist ON.

They stand a short distance outside the reach of a melee attack and press it.

Their fighter immediately faces the opponent, spends the existing Energy cost, plays its mouvment animation while physically closing only the required distance, then starts the real melee attack.

While travelling, pressing a different melee attack changes the pending move so the newest melee is the one that comes out.

While travelling, Jump, normal mouvement/Dash, Shield, Deflect, or any non-melee action cancels the assist immediately and takes over according to the normal rules.

If the target is already in melee range, the attack happens normally without assist or Energy cost.

If the target is too far away, the attack happens normally and may whiff; Combat Assist does not pull the player across the stage.

Projectile/ranged attacks never receive assistance.

CPU fighters never receive assistance under any mode.

Turning Combat Assist OFF restores the existing combat behavior without otherwise changing movement, attacks, Energy, CPU behavior, or input.

The setting defaults ON, persists correctly, migrates existing users safely, appears under Settings → Combat in English and French, and the complete node --test suite passes.

Keep the implementation small, shared, deterministic, data-driven, and consistent with Alva’s existing architecture. Do not solve this by adding fighter-specific conditions, cloning attacks, extending hitboxes, teleporting fighters, or teaching the CPU to use the mechanic.
